A||||4||Black88GT||Cleaning dirty K&N||||1||
Z||000000||Black88GT||12-22-2000||09:44 PM||||Sorry to dedicate a thread to this, but I have a diry K&N that needs cleaning.  I would rather not use the 10 dollar "recharging" kit, is there anything else you can use?  The outside isnt dirty but the inside of the filter is.  Can I just wash it off with water?<P><BR>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000001||WampusCat||12-22-2000||10:03 PM||||Use the recharging kit.  It will clean and re-oil the filter many times.  Plain water wont get the dirty oil out of the cotton.  Most grease cutting detergents will shrink or damage the cotton.  Use the recharging kit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||12-22-2000||10:59 PM||||Ok I guess I will just give in and buy the damn kit.  There I go being a typical cheap Fiero owner.... lol<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000003||sombre||12-22-2000||11:13 PM||||  Can't get much cheaper than the kit.I don't have a K&N in my fiero yet but I do in 2 quads,my amigo,and truck.one kit will do them all at least once.I clean the quad one every month or so in the summer.I'd say you could do the fiero one 4 or 5 times at least.divide that 10 bucks up 5 ways still cheaper than paper.<P>  BTW How did you get the inside dirty and not the outside???<P>                                  Greg||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||12-23-2000||12:18 AM||||The V-6 Fiero air filter system is "backwards" from most other cars.....the dirty air flows from the inside to the outside of the filter.  The result is a filter that looks clean from the outside, but is actually clogged on the inside.<P>I sold that K&N to Jeff and didn't clean it (I should have)......sorry Jeff!   What you need to do is tap the filter with the palm of one hand to shake the large deposits off, then soak it in the cleaner that comes with the recharge kit and rinse in cold water (from the outside to the inside).....you may need to repeat this process.   Let it air dry overnight then reoil it with the K&N oil and you're done.<P>Buy the smallest recharge kit possible.....a little bit goes a long way.  I still have oil and cleaner from a kit I bought 7 years ago!<BR>||||reg||1
